 home services industries. It also develops the QuinStreet Rating Platform product for insurance agents and the CloudControlMedia that provides performance marketing agency and technology services to clients in financial services, education, and other markets. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Foster City, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Douglas  Valenti | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $604,750 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $119K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["QuinStreet, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.1B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 11% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $128M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.62\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 8.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 60% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6047538574393928},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17423896.73},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Communication Services peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"QuinStreet, Inc. $QNST Stock Sold by Royce & Associates LP","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/quinstreet-inc-qnst-stock-sold-by-r